A||||4||86SE||Whats the purpose of the O2 Sensor??||||5||
Z||000000||86SE||01-13-2000||11:53 PM||||My computer has the code for O2 Sensor triggered, but I havent noticed anything terribly wrong with my engine.....Whats the purpose of the O2 sensor anyways, if its just a "sensor" do I need to replace it??||||reg||5
Z||000001||Luperman||01-14-2000||12:24 AM||||The O2 sensor is to measure the exhaust to see if it is too rich or lean and tells the ecm accordly, just because you get the code does not necessarily mean it is your O2 sensor is bad. if your car is running ok try  disconnecting the neg battery terminal to clear any logged codes and see if it will set one again. My .02$||||reg||1
Z||000002||Phaeton||01-14-2000||01:55 AM||||If your O2 sensor did quit then the ECM defaults to full rich, just like driving around with the choke on.  Milage goes way down and the converter can't keep up with the unburned gas (if you have the converter hooked up).||||reg||1
Z||000003||Voyd||01-14-2000||07:32 PM||||how do uknow, or how can u tell if its running full rich?  am getting bad gas mileage, but no codes are being set. i dont even know what the 02 sensor looks like.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Shiner||01-14-2000||11:00 PM||||I get terrible gas mileage in my '87 GT (we are talking chevy big block territory here...), and it sets a code if I cruise on the "naughty" side of the speedometer.  The code stays on until I shut the car down, but I can't find any codes when I run diagnostic!?!  Think it could be my o2 sensor?  ||||reg||1
